  "body": "## What changed\n\nTurning kinds now read the setup bar, so a bar wider than the part can be roughed.\n\n- New `operation/turning_stock.rs` reads the stock's widest radius about the fitted axis and passes it as `StockEnv` (`motion/src/turning/stock.rs`) to `*_in(.., stock)` kernel variants. The old functions call them with `None`, so they're unchanged.\n- Profile rough and finish, groove rough and finish, part, thread and form approach and retract at the bar OD + 1.0 mm radial clearance (plus the nose for an insert). Profile rough counts passes from the bar OD down to the part + leave. Groove rough and part step down from the OD.\n- It only applies when the bar is wider than the part, so snug bars post exactly as today.\n- With no readable stock, the part-based path stands with a named note.\n- Not changed: Facing (#122, an outside contributor's claim), chamfer, taper and multi-pass rides, and bore (already centred; a too-small hole stays refused by #103's law).\n- Parting moved to `turning/parting.rs` for the 400-line limit.\n- `turning_profile.rs`'s 40 mm box stock moved to bar-sized stock, as #103 did for the other fixtures.\n- The 1.0 mm clearance is a constant for now (`STOCK_CLEARANCE`); a per-op parameter is a follow-up.\n\n## Pins\n\n- `turning_axial_rapids::a_rough_in_a_wider_bar_approaches_from_the_bar_and_posts_clean` (20 mm bar → 12 mm part): **fails on main**, where the approach at r 7.9 is inside the bar\n- `turning_stock_approach::a_groove_in_a_wider_bar_…`, `a_parting_cut_in_a_wider_bar_…`: **fail on main**\n- `turning_stock_approach::with_no_stock_the_rough_is_the_part_based_path_and_says_so`\n- motion `turning_stock` (3)\n\n## Readings\n\n- **Green:** all motion turning suites and all app turning and lathe suites, plus drill_prior, posting and golden_cl (23, no golden changed).\n- **Red, not from this PR:** lathe_field_sim's rough/finish test, which fails identically on main (#186). Clippy on motion and app is clean.\n\nChangelog: Turning kinds (profile rough/finish, groove, part, thread, form) approach and retract clear of a setup bar wider than the part, and roughing steps down from the bar's OD - a 20 mm bar can now be roughed to a 12 mm part and posted\n\nFixes #130\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
